> ## 3. A more defensive pattern
> 
> Given how fragile this is, I’d do:
> 
> ```python
> tp = ds['tp']
> 
> # Confirm dask thinks this is small:
> print(tp.chunks)   # should be something like ((1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1),)
> 
> # Find index of non-NaN without computing all of tp:
> # (uses dask's lazy operations)
> mask = tp.notnull()
> idx_da = mask.argmax(dim='region')  # gives index of first True
> 
> # Compute that one small index
> idx = int(idx_da.compute().item())
> 
> # Now extract that element
> val_da = tp.isel(region=idx)
> val = float(val_da.compute().item())
> print(idx, ds['region'].values[idx], val)
> ```
> 
> This still might fail if the upstream graph is pathological, but it minimizes the amount of work.
